WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:06.142
Stanford, and Stanford GSB's
executive education program has

00:00:06.142 --> 00:00:10.463
a very distinctive philosophy
of leadership education.

00:00:10.463 --> 00:00:15.263
We really think that the best leaders
blend the analytical and the intuitive,

00:00:15.263 --> 00:00:20.890
our program is really good at giving you
strengths and both of those dimensions.

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:25.128
One of the most powerful things about our
programs is the ability to rethink your

00:00:25.128 --> 00:00:29.127
challenges and rethink your problems and
call back to your organization.

00:00:29.127 --> 00:00:31.670
And help people in your
organization think about and

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:34.110
approach their challenges
really differently.

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:38.320
Here in Stanford, we believe that
who teaches you really matters.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:43.840
I think that's really the secret sauce,
is that we have these scientists, right?

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:45.932
Who are going to help you
think like a scientist.

00:00:45.932 --> 00:00:48.508
They're going to help you
break down your problems and

00:00:48.508 --> 00:00:51.760
think about your problems
in a different way.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.750
Oftentimes, leadership is lonely.

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:58.343
You have problems in your organization
that you can't solve by talking to

00:00:58.343 --> 00:01:00.277
people in your organization.

00:01:00.277 --> 00:01:04.740
One of the most valuable things you
get out of an executive education

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:08.810
program here at Stanford is
a group of fellow participants who

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:11.488
have been through the same experience.

00:01:11.488 --> 00:01:13.331
They've developed the same language.

00:01:13.331 --> 00:01:15.860
They have the same frameworks, and

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:19.749
they can become your trusted
advisors going forward.

00:01:19.749 --> 00:01:23.996
Joining an executive education program
it's a big investment of time and

00:01:23.996 --> 00:01:24.755
resources.

00:01:24.755 --> 00:01:29.336
What I can tell you is that everybody
I've met who's made that decision and

00:01:29.336 --> 00:01:33.857
has come to Stanford and gone through
our programs has been transformed.

00:01:33.857 --> 00:01:38.642
My hope for people who come through these
programs is always that they leave.

00:01:38.642 --> 00:01:39.834
[MUSIC]

00:01:39.834 --> 00:01:45.825
Thinking differently about themselves,
thinking differently about their jobs,

00:01:45.825 --> 00:01:49.550
thinking differently about
their organizations.

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:53.137
And most importantly thinking
differently about how they're going to

00:01:53.137 --> 00:01:54.133
change the world.

00:01:54.133 --> 00:01:56.900
[MUSIC]

